Kahan summation is unnecessary here and costs a serial dependency chain. The transform is affine and bounded, so a plain float32 accumulation is accurate enough; the main win is exposing parallelism. With `threads_per_row=32`, each thread strides over columns and a small tree reduction combines partials, giving 32× more threads and a much shorter serial chain while preserving the required ABI and dispatch contract.

